1
00:00:48,910 --> 00:00:54,380
Miss Peregrine's Home for Peculiar Children

2
00:02:44,530 --> 00:02:47,830
You ever feel like nothing you do matters?

3
00:02:48,700 --> 00:02:53,000
You leave footprints on the beach and somehow they are gone

4
00:02:53,440 --> 00:02:56,640
Like its just today, over again.

5
00:02:57,240 --> 00:03:00,910
They say that your teen years are for making friends and having fun.

6
00:03:01,340 --> 00:03:03,740
Which made me feel even worse

7
00:03:04,210 --> 00:03:08,150
Hey, Amy. It's Jake. I'm in your math class.

8
00:03:08,950 --> 00:03:11,620
Hey do not forget your adult diapers. Yeah right.

9
00:03:18,760 --> 00:03:19,890
Jake

10
00:03:20,600 --> 00:03:21,960
Its a phone for you.

11
00:03:22,400 --> 00:03:25,670
But that day, everything changed

12
00:03:27,940 --> 00:03:29,740
Thanks for the ride, Shelly.

13
00:03:30,510 --> 00:03:32,970
How come you have to go deal with your grandpa?

14
00:03:33,410 --> 00:03:35,640
My dad, couldn't get out of work

15
00:03:36,080 --> 00:03:38,710
I didn't think he worked.

16
00:03:40,420 --> 00:03:44,920
You know, I'm...I'm just gonna call grandpa.

17
00:03:47,590 --> 00:03:49,120
Hello, this is Abe

18
00:03:49,520 --> 00:03:50,590
Hey, it's Jake.

19
00:03:50,890 --> 00:03:52,430
No, don't come here.

20
00:03:52,760 --> 00:03:53,990
Listen to me.

21
00:03:54,400 --> 00:03:55,830
Its not safe!

22
00:03:56,100 --> 00:03:57,360
Stay away.

23
00:03:57,630 --> 00:03:59,630
Grandpa, did you take your pills today?

24
00:03:59,970 --> 00:04:01,270
The Key!

25
00:04:01,540 --> 00:04:03,700
To my gun cabinet... it was in the drawer

26
00:04:03,940 --> 00:04:05,370
And now its gone!

27
00:04:06,140 --> 00:04:08,140
Yeah, Dad took it.

28
00:04:08,440 --> 00:04:10,210
A'right? For safekeeping.

29
00:04:10,480 --> 00:04:11,680
It's okay.

30
00:04:11,950 --> 00:04:15,220
Your father wants, I should to fight them without a gun?!

31
00:04:19,920 --> 00:04:21,790
God bless him.

32
00:04:22,420 --> 00:04:24,260
Whats his deal? Alzheimers?

33
00:04:24,630 --> 00:04:26,260
Dementia

34
00:04:46,210 --> 00:04:48,750
That guy gave me the heebie-jeebies.

35
00:04:58,630 --> 00:05:00,660
Holler if you need me.

36
00:05:08,170 --> 00:05:09,740
Grandpa!

37
00:05:34,330 --> 00:05:35,800
Shelly!

38
00:05:40,970 --> 00:05:42,270
What's going on?

39
00:05:42,640 --> 00:05:43,970
Someone broke in!

40
00:05:44,340 --> 00:05:47,270
I have a .38 in my car, you wait there.

41
00:06:49,670 --> 00:06:52,016
911, what is your emergency? 911? Yeah I...I need

42
00:06:52,028 --> 00:06:55,040
the para-medics to 2040 Palm Circle.

43
00:06:55,610 --> 00:06:56,840
My grandpa...

44
00:06:57,350 --> 00:07:01,380
Grandpa. You have to get away from here

45
00:07:02,380 --> 00:07:04,150
Please, listen.

46
00:07:04,690 --> 00:07:07,190
Go to the Island...

47
00:07:08,390 --> 00:07:10,960
Find Emerson...

48
00:07:12,030 --> 00:07:18,370
The postcard... go to the loop... September 3rd, 1943.

49
00:07:18,900 --> 00:07:21,940
Its okay, just... just don't move. There's an ambulance coming.

50
00:07:22,470 --> 00:07:28,840
I know you think I'm crazy. But the bird will explain everything.

51
00:07:29,510 --> 00:07:32,350
Will you do this Tegrisco? promise me?

52
00:07:32,750 --> 00:07:34,350
I promise, yes..

53
00:07:35,020 --> 00:07:37,250
I thought I could protect you.

54
00:07:39,090 --> 00:07:42,920
I should have told you years ago

55
00:07:49,530 --> 00:07:52,070
Grandpa! Tell me...tell me what?

56
00:07:52,600 --> 00:07:54,170
GRANDPA!

57
00:08:13,820 --> 00:08:16,490
Shelly behind you!  

58
00:08:29,800 --> 00:08:32,940
There was no one there.

59
00:08:33,910 --> 00:08:38,050
May I say Jake.... that considering that this was just a month ago

60
00:08:38,380 --> 00:08:41,180
I think you're doing exceptionally well.

61
00:08:41,650 --> 00:08:44,280
Apart from being crazy?

62
00:08:44,950 --> 00:08:48,090
Having nightmares and anxiety doesn't make you crazy.

63
00:08:48,520 --> 00:08:50,960
And what about seeing things which aren't there?

64
00:08:51,360 --> 00:08:54,330
Actually in dramatic situations its not at all uncommon.

65
00:08:54,830 --> 00:08:57,030
Your subconscious mind draws an image from a movie, or....

66
00:08:57,700 --> 00:08:59,630
It was a story.

67
00:09:00,900 --> 00:09:03,370
My grandpa told me stories when I was a kid

68
00:09:03,940 --> 00:09:06,170
About monsters that he fought in the war

69
00:09:06,240 --> 00:09:07,270
So there you go.

70
00:09:07,810 --> 00:09:11,580
He was brutally attacked. And in your head the man who did it was inhuman.

71
00:09:11,950 --> 00:09:12,950
A monster.

72
00:09:13,420 --> 00:09:15,150
It wasn't a man though.

73
00:09:16,020 --> 00:09:19,920
The cops said that dogs scratched up the screen door.

74
00:09:20,360 --> 00:09:22,760
And he chased them off into the woods

75
00:09:23,320 --> 00:09:26,190
And the coroner said he had a heart attack

76
00:09:26,530 --> 00:09:28,530
And the cops said

77
00:09:30,070 --> 00:09:32,570
dogs went for the soft parts.

78
00:09:33,900 --> 00:09:38,010
The DNA had wounds of animals

79
00:09:38,440 --> 00:09:40,940
so thats case closed.

80
00:09:41,780 --> 00:09:44,550
He sounds like an extraordinary gentleman.

81
00:09:45,150 --> 00:09:47,250
Were you very close?

82
00:09:47,650 --> 00:09:48,950
Puerto Rico.

83
00:09:49,280 --> 00:09:50,650
Here

84
00:09:51,350 --> 00:09:54,290
There is a lake where the water glows in the dark.

85
00:09:54,960 --> 00:09:58,730
And a secret tunnel. Thats where I hid from the monsters

86
00:09:59,230 --> 00:10:01,500
He used to babysit me a lot.

87
00:10:02,160 --> 00:10:05,070
And when I was with him I felt special.

88
00:10:07,340 --> 00:10:08,570
Abe.

89
00:10:09,070 --> 00:10:11,870
Its like 11 o'clock. What is he doin up?

90
00:10:12,640 --> 00:10:17,210
Im going to be an explorer. Grandpas told me about my first voyage.

91
00:10:17,750 --> 00:10:20,750
Everything has already been discovered, buddy.

92
00:10:25,220 --> 00:10:31,130
Pay no attention to your father. He knows bubkiss. Come tegrisco... off to bed.

93
00:10:40,700 --> 00:10:42,270
Can you tell me a story

94
00:10:42,540 --> 00:10:43,700
The usual?

95
00:10:44,410 --> 00:10:46,070
Okay

96
00:10:46,780 --> 00:10:49,780
Once upon a time there was a little boy

97
00:10:50,150 --> 00:10:52,080
where's the pictures?

98
00:10:52,780 --> 00:10:53,880
Pictures.

99
00:11:01,020 --> 00:11:04,930
Once upon a time a little boy called Abe

100
00:11:05,360 --> 00:11:06,790
That was you.

101
00:11:07,130 --> 00:11:13,870
That was me and he lived in a lovely children's home on an little island near Wales.

102
00:11:14,370 --> 00:11:16,740
Where the sun shone every day.

103
00:11:17,270 --> 00:11:19,770
The Headmistress, Miss Peregrine....

104
00:11:20,180 --> 00:11:22,180
Was very clever.

105
00:11:22,640 --> 00:11:24,110
and she smoked my pipe

106
00:11:24,480 --> 00:11:26,750
She could turn into a bird

107
00:11:27,650 --> 00:11:30,680
It was a home for special children

108
00:11:31,350 --> 00:11:33,090
Like Bronwyn...

109
00:11:33,520 --> 00:11:35,360
and Victor

110
00:11:36,060 --> 00:11:38,960
They were both as strong as ten men.

111
00:11:39,430 --> 00:11:40,660
And Hugh

112
00:11:41,030 --> 00:11:44,930
Hugh had bees living inside him.

113
00:11:45,370 --> 00:11:48,070
Where is Emma? She could float.

114
00:11:48,970 --> 00:11:52,140
She was lighter than air.

115
00:11:52,810 --> 00:11:58,150
She had to wear special shoes made of lead 
to keep her from floating away.

116
00:11:58,580 --> 00:12:00,310
Where is she now?

117
00:12:00,680 --> 00:12:02,080
She's still on the Island, I believe

118
00:12:03,550 --> 00:12:08,120
My mom and papa sent me there, to live with the special children.

119
00:12:08,560 --> 00:12:11,760
And now Tegrisco time to sleep.

120
00:12:12,160 --> 00:12:13,790
He used to call me Tegrisco.

121
00:12:14,160 --> 00:12:16,330
Its Polish, for little tiger. 

122
00:12:16,770 --> 00:12:20,300
Couldn't have picked a less appropriate nickname,
 I was always a chicken.

123
00:12:20,700 --> 00:12:23,500
Why your mom and dad send you away?

124
00:12:24,110 --> 00:12:27,610
Where we lived in Poland, it was not safe.

125
00:12:28,280 --> 00:12:29,880
There were monsters.

126
00:12:30,250 --> 00:12:32,150
What kind of monsters?

127
00:12:32,580 --> 00:12:34,350
Huge ones.

128
00:12:34,820 --> 00:12:42,160
With long arms and no eyes. And tentacles like this.

129
00:12:44,060 --> 00:12:49,030
The dumb thing was, for years I actually believed his stories

130
00:12:50,270 --> 00:12:52,970
This is Millard, he's invisible.

131
00:12:59,370 --> 00:13:02,110
My teacher says they are trick photos.

132
00:13:03,140 --> 00:13:05,210
And did you believe her?

133
00:13:06,050 --> 00:13:10,380
Dad says that you get in one of those places that you were traveling.

134
00:13:10,990 --> 00:13:13,550
I would never lie to you, Tegrisco.

135
00:13:13,990 --> 00:13:15,560
But you did it.

136
00:13:16,120 --> 00:13:18,630
About the home... the monsters.

137
00:13:19,930 --> 00:13:21,730
Dad told me.

138
00:13:22,360 --> 00:13:26,470
Your father knows very well that I went to live in the children's home

139
00:13:27,270 --> 00:13:30,270
He said there were monsters in Poland

140
00:13:30,870 --> 00:13:33,910
Just not the kind with tentacles.

141
00:13:34,640 --> 00:13:37,780
He said you got sent away to Wales because there were bad people.

142
00:13:38,180 --> 00:13:42,620
People who wanted to kill anyone who was different

143
00:13:43,150 --> 00:13:45,420
I do not want to talk about this anymore.

144
00:13:45,890 --> 00:13:48,720
He said children were special

145
00:13:49,320 --> 00:13:53,330
but not the way you said.

146
00:14:30,200 --> 00:14:32,000
You find something good?

147
00:14:33,330 --> 00:14:34,940
Aw. Look at that.

148
00:14:35,270 --> 00:14:36,700
It's awesome.

149
00:14:37,110 --> 00:14:38,610
Take that

150
00:14:39,010 --> 00:14:41,140
C'mon buddy, lets roll.

151
00:14:41,780 --> 00:14:44,180
How are you so okay?

152
00:14:45,380 --> 00:14:48,120
Jake, You were a lot closer to him than I ever was

153
00:14:48,720 --> 00:14:52,020
He was a wonderful grandpa. But not...not such a great dad, you know?.

154
00:14:54,620 --> 00:14:59,230
Never seemed to pick a job that didn't involve late nights and long trips away though.

155
00:14:59,930 --> 00:15:04,470
Me and Aunt Sussie I always kinda thought he was maybe cheating on our mom.

156
00:15:06,770 --> 00:15:12,010
I am sorry, buddy. I know how much you worshipped him but there it is.

157
00:15:19,310 --> 00:15:20,880
Surprise!!

158
00:15:21,250 --> 00:15:22,720
Happy Birthday. cousin Jake.

159
00:15:23,320 --> 00:15:25,126
Jake, its great you've to come to spend the summer with us.

160
00:15:25,150 --> 00:15:26,820
Wait till you see the new dogs

161
00:15:27,160 --> 00:15:28,660
Can't wait.

162
00:15:38,270 --> 00:15:40,000
Its aunt Sussie.

163
00:15:40,500 --> 00:15:42,740
Thought you might want to open this one.

164
00:15:43,670 --> 00:15:45,770
Its from your grandpa

165
00:15:46,270 --> 00:15:50,280
Found it while I was packing up. I figured he meant to give it to you someday.

166
00:15:53,150 --> 00:15:53,950
Thanks

167
00:16:02,720 --> 00:16:08,360
"Complete Essays and other writings of Ralph Waldo Emerson."

168
00:16:11,570 --> 00:16:18,310
To Jake and the worlds he has yet to discover

169
00:16:27,150 --> 00:16:28,650
My dearest Abe. "

170
00:16:29,020 --> 00:16:31,250
I hope this card finds you well

171
00:16:31,590 --> 00:16:34,320
The children and I yearn to hear your news.

172
00:16:34,660 --> 00:16:36,820
I do hope you will visit us again soon

173
00:16:37,160 --> 00:16:38,860
We should so love to see you."

174
00:16:39,190 --> 00:16:42,400
With admiration, Alma Peregrine. "

175
00:16:42,830 --> 00:16:44,570
Hmm... Only two years ago

176
00:16:44,900 --> 00:16:47,570
I suppose its possible she could still be still be alive.

177
00:16:48,000 --> 00:16:49,070
Right

178
00:16:49,700 --> 00:16:51,410
And I could meet her.

179
00:16:52,110 --> 00:16:54,840
Maybe even find out what it was Grandpa wanted me to know.

180
00:16:55,180 --> 00:16:56,540
But what if she's dead?

181
00:16:56,880 --> 00:17:00,110
Dr. Golan, we are very concerned with Jake's state of mind right now

182
00:17:00,450 --> 00:17:03,880
And there is no way I'm putting my life on hold to take you to Wales.

183
00:17:04,420 --> 00:17:06,150
Dad could take me.

184
00:17:06,760 --> 00:17:10,360
And he can even look at birds... work in his book

185
00:17:10,760 --> 00:17:12,760
It means you get a break.

186
00:17:13,230 --> 00:17:17,230
And as Dr. Golan said. Maybe I can move on.

187
00:17:17,670 --> 00:17:19,430
Like closure.

188
00:17:20,300 --> 00:17:25,240
Having an opportunity to see this Children's Home and separate fantasy from reality,

189
00:17:25,570 --> 00:17:31,380
May be useful and at the very least a trip like this provides a chance to

190
00:17:31,780 --> 00:17:34,380
say goodbye

191
00:17:39,250 --> 00:17:45,590
Cairnholm: population of 92. Best known for its proximity to the final resting place of the cruise liner 

192
00:17:46,190 --> 00:17:50,860
Augusta which sank in 1915.

193
00:17:51,370 --> 00:17:52,930
There is only one hotel

194
00:17:53,330 --> 00:17:55,040
Thats us

195
00:17:55,470 --> 00:17:58,070
Be sure *********

196
00:18:00,440 --> 00:18:04,080
Oh wow! Jake! check it out. That's a peregrine falcon.

197
00:18:04,880 --> 00:18:07,680
Peregrine, like the Headmistress?

198
00:18:08,050 --> 00:18:09,280
Sure

199
00:18:09,880 --> 00:18:13,520
Hey thats probably where grandpa came with the tale of turning into a bird thing.

200
00:18:13,990 --> 00:18:16,360
Maybe. Maybe that's really her.

201
00:18:16,960 --> 00:18:22,260
"Hey Ms. Peregrine, Its me Jake I am Abe Portman's grandson.

202
00:18:22,700 --> 00:18:25,600
Please don't crap on us"

203
00:18:26,800 --> 00:18:30,170
Oh. god, Dad I'm kidding

204
00:18:56,030 --> 00:18:57,660
What the h....Hello?

205
00:18:59,130 --> 00:19:00,700
Hello?

206
00:19:05,210 --> 00:19:07,640
Anybody home?

207
00:19:09,440 --> 00:19:12,880
"Two Torpedoes hit RMS Augusta 894 lost"

208
00:19:18,150 --> 00:19:21,420
Oh Hey! Any idea where I'd find the manager of this place?

209
00:19:21,790 --> 00:19:22,790
That's me

210
00:19:23,020 --> 00:19:26,100
Sorry to keep you. Just helping uncle Oggie to the loo

211
00:19:26,930 --> 00:19:29,560
I'm Kev. There's room upstairs. Great

212
00:19:29,960 --> 00:19:31,900
I'll be back in a bit.

213
00:19:33,000 --> 00:19:35,770
Kev's jus gettin our suite ready.

214
00:19:36,370 --> 00:19:39,740
While we are waiting, I thought maybe we could go check out the beach.

215
00:19:40,310 --> 00:19:42,310
I thought we'd go to the Children's Home.

216
00:19:42,780 --> 00:19:44,710
It the beach where the birds nest?

217
00:19:45,150 --> 00:19:46,910
I...I thought we could check it out real quick

218
00:19:47,550 --> 00:19:49,580
I could go to the home by myself.

219
00:19:50,120 --> 00:19:52,590
And you can, really take your time.

220
00:19:52,950 --> 00:19:53,950
And I enjoy it

221
00:19:54,290 --> 00:19:57,020
Come on. Jakey. You know your mom would freak.

222
00:19:57,560 --> 00:19:59,660
What if we can find someone to take me?

223
00:20:01,460 --> 00:20:03,130
Hey dudes

224
00:20:04,000 --> 00:20:05,170
Dad! I got this

225
00:20:05,570 --> 00:20:08,516
I was just wondering if any of you guys might be interested in taking my son

226
00:20:08,540 --> 00:20:10,440
here, to the other side of the island.

227
00:20:24,290 --> 00:20:26,020
And what are your names?

228
00:20:26,490 --> 00:20:28,590
I am Worm and this is Epsy Denty.

229
00:20:28,990 --> 00:20:30,220
Epsy Bussines.

230
00:20:30,560 --> 00:20:31,990
I thought you changed that! No!

231
00:20:32,330 --> 00:20:33,630
No. You did remember?

232
00:20:33,960 --> 00:20:37,460
When Lou said Epsy Bussines made it look like cracked trousers.

233
00:20:37,770 --> 00:20:40,210
Yeah, But she said it sounded like a personal hygiene problem.

234
00:20:40,670 --> 00:20:42,840
Wait, Are these are like nicknames or...

235
00:20:43,200 --> 00:20:45,610
stage names of rappers here in Wales.

236
00:20:46,010 --> 00:20:48,310
Come on, Worm, show this shank how its done

237
00:20:48,610 --> 00:20:49,910
What? Now?

238
00:20:50,480 --> 00:20:52,080
I like to throw letters in the churches.

239
00:20:52,380 --> 00:20:53,980
My father is always there, the very dog.

240
00:20:54,220 --> 00:20:55,520
But no one can with me,

241
00:20:55,850 --> 00:20:58,420
I will break the ice like a burning blade.

242
00:20:59,950 --> 00:21:02,360
Yes, it is, it is good.

243
00:21:03,760 --> 00:21:06,130
Should we take the shortcut, D. We'll get there quicker.

244
00:21:06,560 --> 00:21:07,830
Take it from me.

245
00:21:08,630 --> 00:21:09,800
What? Down here?

246
00:21:25,380 --> 00:21:26,580
Yeah

247
00:21:36,060 --> 00:21:38,830
Is this even the way to the Children's home?

248
00:21:39,360 --> 00:21:41,760
Right through those trees.

249
00:22:09,060 --> 00:22:12,590
No use cryin' over a lost shoe, boy

250
00:22:16,200 --> 00:22:18,670
The Children's Home... What happened to it?

251
00:22:19,070 --> 00:22:22,400
The German navy A bomb fell right on the roof.

252
00:22:23,000 --> 00:22:25,870
September the 3rd, 1943.

253
00:22:26,370 --> 00:22:28,080
Where... where did they go after it?

254
00:22:28,440 --> 00:22:30,440
The Headmistress and the children?

255
00:22:30,850 --> 00:22:33,010
Not one survivor.

256
00:22:33,420 --> 00:22:36,250
Poor little buggers... and they were lovely too.

257
00:22:37,890 --> 00:22:40,850
Why didn't he tell us that they all died?

258
00:22:41,420 --> 00:22:45,960
He leaves to join the army and three months everyone he knows gets killed?

259
00:22:46,590 --> 00:22:50,300
Not even grandpa can turn that into a bedtime story

260
00:22:50,770 --> 00:22:53,600
No wonder he was scared at being a dad.

261
00:22:54,000 --> 00:22:56,370
Being close to anyone.

262
00:22:57,310 --> 00:22:59,170
Listen.

263
00:22:59,740 --> 00:23:01,940
if you need to talk about all this with someone, buddy.

264
00:23:02,740 --> 00:23:05,180
We should call Dr. Golan.

265
00:23:13,350 --> 00:23:16,760
Do you mind if I go hang out with those other kids today?

266
00:23:17,890 --> 00:23:19,190
They asked.

267
00:23:19,590 --> 00:23:21,300
Yeah. That's awesome

268
00:24:55,760 --> 00:24:57,420
Abe?

269
00:25:46,170 --> 00:25:47,670
You're Emma

270
00:25:48,310 --> 00:25:50,010
And the twins.

271
00:25:50,550 --> 00:25:51,950
And Olive

272
00:25:52,350 --> 00:25:53,980
Bromwin

273
00:25:54,820 --> 00:25:56,420
He's Miller.

274
00:25:57,190 --> 00:25:58,490
You are dead

275
00:25:58,790 --> 00:26:00,490
All of you. You're all dead

276
00:26:01,120 --> 00:26:03,560
I mean he is...he is invisible he's still dead

277
00:26:04,030 --> 00:26:06,360
None of us are dead

278
00:26:07,030 --> 00:26:08,430
[Oh my God] Am I dead?

279
00:26:09,000 --> 00:26:10,230
No

280
00:26:12,530 --> 00:26:16,000
You called me Abe, in the house. Why?

281
00:26:16,600 --> 00:26:18,170
You look like him.

282
00:26:18,570 --> 00:26:19,870
Just for a moment

283
00:26:20,280 --> 00:26:23,710
Before you started screaming, running away and concussing yourself.

284
00:26:24,150 --> 00:26:25,650
Wait, what's happening?

285
00:26:26,080 --> 00:26:29,180
We are waiting until the coast is clear before we go into the loop.

286
00:26:29,850 --> 00:26:32,250
You never know who might be watching.

287
00:26:32,820 --> 00:26:35,160
Wait, before we...before we go into what?

288
00:26:35,520 --> 00:26:41,130
Please Jake Ms. peregrine's waiting. She saw on the ferry and sent us to get you.

289
00:27:32,280 --> 00:27:34,110
Where do you think you're going?

290
00:27:34,920 --> 00:27:36,650
To my room

291
00:27:38,250 --> 00:27:39,920
Im a...I am a guest here

292
00:27:40,520 --> 00:27:43,560
Does this look like a hotel to you?

293
00:27:45,230 --> 00:27:47,130
Yeah...No!.

294
00:27:48,060 --> 00:27:49,730
I've....I've got a key.

295
00:27:49,860 --> 00:27:52,470
Talk to the manager. He'll tell you.

296
00:27:53,030 --> 00:27:54,700
I'm the manager, boy.

297
00:27:55,040 --> 00:27:56,100
He's American.

298
00:27:56,440 --> 00:27:57,770
Maybe he's army?

299
00:27:58,070 --> 00:28:01,280
Bollocks! Listen to his accent. It's terrible!

300
00:28:02,280 --> 00:28:04,040
He is a spy.

301
00:28:04,980 --> 00:28:06,080
What?

302
00:28:06,480 --> 00:28:08,780
No, I'm not I'm a tourist

303
00:28:09,480 --> 00:28:13,290
I say, we should get the truth out of him - the old-fashioned way.

304
00:28:47,060 --> 00:28:49,620
Come on, quick guys.

305
00:28:59,630 --> 00:29:01,370
I can't believe you're real.

306
00:29:01,770 --> 00:29:02,770
You're all real

307
00:29:03,100 --> 00:29:04,416
We've been trying to tell you.

308
00:29:04,440 --> 00:29:05,560
But I am special too.

309
00:29:05,710 --> 00:29:06,710
What?

310
00:29:06,980 --> 00:29:08,610
In the pub all of you saw it. Right?

311
00:29:08,980 --> 00:29:12,850
Everything was flying and breaking. And that was me.

312
00:29:13,210 --> 00:29:15,150
I was doing it with my mind.

313
00:29:15,520 --> 00:29:17,450
No, that was me

314
00:29:18,290 --> 00:29:19,620
Miller? Yeah.

315
00:29:22,260 --> 00:29:23,920
Are you naked? Yeah

316
00:29:31,330 --> 00:29:33,930
A bomb drops on you in 1943.

317
00:29:34,300 --> 00:29:35,940
It is 1943

318
00:29:36,370 --> 00:29:38,870
September the 3rd, 1943

319
00:29:39,270 --> 00:29:41,010
The whole day, every day

320
00:29:41,280 --> 00:29:42,940
Its our loop

321
00:30:14,540 --> 00:30:16,840
Right on time

322
00:30:17,510 --> 00:30:19,910
Ms. Peregrine. Delighted to meet you.

323
00:30:20,520 --> 00:30:23,880
I do hope Im not going to have the pub landlord knocking 
on my door with the police again?

324
00:30:24,290 --> 00:30:26,350
I've had to kill them twice this month

325
00:30:26,650 --> 00:30:28,220
Its been terribly inconvenient.

326
00:30:28,560 --> 00:30:30,520
We may have broken some things, that's all.

327
00:30:31,230 --> 00:30:34,600
And Olive may have started a tiny fire

328
00:30:35,400 --> 00:30:37,900
But they were going to hurt Jake.

329
00:30:41,340 --> 00:30:42,840
Look at you!

330
00:30:43,540 --> 00:30:47,410
The last time dear Abe sent me a photograph, 
you were a just a tiny todd.

331
00:30:47,880 --> 00:30:49,110
Don't you stand there, come in.

332
00:30:49,480 --> 00:30:51,310
Your tea is getting cold.

333
00:30:53,110 --> 00:30:55,180
How did you know about the pub?

334
00:30:55,680 --> 00:30:57,820
Your weigh approximately a 109 pounds, correct?

335
00:30:58,390 --> 00:31:00,950
Bronwyn and the twins returned six minutes after you ran away.

336
00:31:01,260 --> 00:31:02,390
I think Im missing something.

337
00:31:02,560 --> 00:31:05,890
And quite apart from the fact that the perceived safety of the pub 
makes it...

338
00:31:06,230 --> 00:31:07,860
the most likely place to which you would flee?

339
00:31:08,160 --> 00:31:09,760
It would take you 18 minutes to run there.

340
00:31:10,030 --> 00:31:13,800
Emma and Miller would have been moments behind with the 
horse and trap travelling at around 8.2 miles per hour.

341
00:31:14,240 --> 00:31:18,510
Fact doing some sort of Kerfuffle in the pub and 
the return journey with your added weight.

342
00:31:19,010 --> 00:31:21,980
You would arrive here with 30 minutes past 4

343
00:31:22,480 --> 00:31:24,480
now then, do you like sugar?

344
00:31:25,680 --> 00:31:29,320
That will be enough, thank you Olive. Nobody enjoys overboiled tea.

345
00:31:39,560 --> 00:31:41,800
Let me help you, Enoch.

346
00:31:42,100 --> 00:31:43,330
Do not bother.

347
00:31:43,730 --> 00:31:46,400
Wouldn't want you to interrupt the tea party.

348
00:31:54,580 --> 00:31:56,910
I'm so sorry for your loss, Jake.

349
00:31:58,350 --> 00:32:00,310
You know, then?

350
00:32:01,550 --> 00:32:03,220
I know if Abe were alive

351
00:32:03,550 --> 00:32:05,920
You would have told me you were coming.

352
00:32:08,260 --> 00:32:10,890
Shall we take our tea outside?

353
00:32:14,800 --> 00:32:17,700
Before he died he told me to find you.

354
00:32:18,070 --> 00:32:20,600
There was something he wanted me to know

355
00:32:20,900 --> 00:32:22,540
He said you could explain everything.

356
00:32:22,840 --> 00:32:26,410
That's absolutely true. But there are few things I can't explain

357
00:32:26,740 --> 00:32:30,740
We are in common parlance - as peculiar

358
00:32:32,810 --> 00:32:34,820
51 seconds late, Fiona.

359
00:32:35,180 --> 00:32:36,450
Sorry Ms. Peregrine

360
00:32:36,750 --> 00:32:38,350
How many carrots you need for supper?

361
00:32:38,620 --> 00:32:40,420
Just one will do.

362
00:32:54,570 --> 00:32:58,170
As I was saying some people are peculiar

363
00:32:58,570 --> 00:33:01,110
Its a recessive gene carried down through families.

364
00:33:01,740 --> 00:33:06,080
Yet, many generations can pass without a peculiar child being born

365
00:33:06,450 --> 00:33:10,520
And alas, peculiars have been persecuted through the ages

366
00:33:10,920 --> 00:33:13,450
Hence, we live in places like this.

367
00:33:14,320 --> 00:33:15,520
in Wales?

368
00:33:15,890 --> 00:33:17,866
Anywhere will do if you pick the right day.

369
00:33:17,890 --> 00:33:20,730
Thats fine now, Fiona.

370
00:33:24,100 --> 00:33:28,040
You see. I am a type of peculiar called an Ymbryne. That means I can....

371
00:33:28,540 --> 00:33:30,100
You can turn into a bird.

372
00:33:30,310 --> 00:33:33,340
Well I do! But that's not very useful.

373
00:33:33,880 --> 00:33:36,840
An Ymbryne's main skill is the manipulation of time.

374
00:33:37,180 --> 00:33:41,720
We chose a safe place, a safe day and create a loop

375
00:33:41,980 --> 00:33:43,320
What do you mean?

376
00:33:43,750 --> 00:33:46,890
A loop preserves the last 24 hours.

377
00:33:47,220 --> 00:33:50,360
Reset the loop and the day is yours to live in again.

378
00:33:50,690 --> 00:33:53,690
Reset it daily and you can stay there forever

379
00:33:54,130 --> 00:33:56,860
Entirely safe from the outside world

380
00:33:57,330 --> 00:34:00,130
Right on time Bronwyn, good girl

381
00:34:04,510 --> 00:34:09,010
And thats why we Ymbrynes are charged with the care of the young.

382
00:34:11,410 --> 00:34:13,850
And no one ever gets older?

383
00:34:14,220 --> 00:34:16,420
Its best for everyone this way

384
00:34:17,020 --> 00:34:18,420
I assure you.

385
00:34:21,360 --> 00:34:26,090
Each Ymbryne commits herself to the creation and upkeep
 of a place like this

386
00:34:26,530 --> 00:34:29,460
A Home for Peculiar Children.

387
00:34:41,940 --> 00:34:43,940
You've met the twins

388
00:34:49,050 --> 00:34:50,680
This is Claire

389
00:35:02,460 --> 00:35:04,430
Miller you've met

390
00:35:06,630 --> 00:35:09,570
And that's Hugh

391
00:35:12,270 --> 00:35:14,880
Stop cheating Hugh

392
00:35:15,440 --> 00:35:17,480
Miller thats a foul, again!

393
00:35:18,110 --> 00:35:19,410
No it wasn't!

394
00:35:20,920 --> 00:35:24,550
If you two cant play without squabbling, 
wish you wouldn't play at all.

395
00:35:24,990 --> 00:35:26,720
Look who our referee is.

396
00:35:27,360 --> 00:35:30,720
Good afternoon. I'm Horace. Delighted to meet you

397
00:35:32,530 --> 00:35:34,130
We sorely needed some new blood here.

398
00:35:34,960 --> 00:35:37,530
Super shirt by the way

399
00:35:38,000 --> 00:35:39,300
Thanks

400
00:35:43,200 --> 00:35:45,540
You know Emma, of course

401
00:35:46,310 --> 00:35:48,110
And I think thats everyone.

402
00:35:48,880 --> 00:35:51,010
Didn't Bronwyn have a brother?

403
00:35:51,580 --> 00:35:53,710
Yes, Victor's upstairs.

404
00:35:54,350 --> 00:35:56,120
Wait, where did Enoch and Olive go?

405
00:35:56,450 --> 00:35:57,480
Heaven knows.

406
00:35:57,790 --> 00:35:59,950
Enoch's been off ever since we went to look for Jake.

407
00:36:00,360 --> 00:36:03,390
Ms. Peregrine there's a policemen at the door. 
He says it's about the pub.

408
00:36:04,890 --> 00:36:09,000
We discuss this later, Emma.

409
00:36:09,400 --> 00:36:11,430
It wasn't their fault

410
00:36:12,030 --> 00:36:15,070
Honestly, just they were just trying to help

411
00:36:24,350 --> 00:36:27,550
Thanks. You're not as vet as I thought

412
00:36:30,890 --> 00:36:33,850
She's not really going to kill anyone, is she?

413
00:36:34,220 --> 00:36:36,320
Not if she can talk her way out of it.

414
00:36:36,720 --> 00:36:38,160
Would you help me with something.

415
00:36:38,630 --> 00:36:41,700
Enoch usually does it but, like I said, he is sulking somewhere.

416
00:36:42,560 --> 00:36:44,260
Is that because of me?

417
00:36:44,700 --> 00:36:46,800
He is possessive

418
00:36:49,100 --> 00:36:51,870
So.... What you need help with?

419
00:36:52,340 --> 00:36:53,570
One of my daily chores.

420
00:36:53,980 --> 00:36:56,140
Put the baby squirrel back in the tree.

421
00:36:56,440 --> 00:36:58,650
What baby squirrel?

422
00:37:03,180 --> 00:37:04,790
That happens every day?

423
00:37:05,090 --> 00:37:06,820
Like clockwork.

424
00:37:07,890 --> 00:37:10,420
Now, would you mind tying that rope around my waist?

425
00:37:12,030 --> 00:37:13,030
Uh...Yeah.

426
00:37:40,390 --> 00:37:42,860
Right. Promise to hold on tight?

427
00:38:27,740 --> 00:38:30,070
I knew we messed that up.

428
00:38:30,140 --> 00:38:32,740
Abe did too... the first time.

429
00:38:33,340 --> 00:38:35,710
This used to be his job

430
00:38:37,410 --> 00:38:40,150
Emma, ​​I need to tell you something.

431
00:38:41,520 --> 00:38:43,580
He is dead.

432
00:38:44,390 --> 00:38:48,060
I know. Ms. Peregrine guessed and she's always right.

433
00:38:49,620 --> 00:38:50,860
It's okay

434
00:38:51,630 --> 00:38:54,390
I said goodbye to him a long time ago

435
00:38:54,830 --> 00:38:57,100
Were you close?

436
00:38:58,270 --> 00:39:00,270
I thought we were.

437
00:39:00,970 --> 00:39:02,670
For a while.

438
00:39:03,140 --> 00:39:05,340
But I suppose not

439
00:39:07,080 --> 00:39:10,710
Can I ask, was he like you?

440
00:39:12,980 --> 00:39:15,820
He was like you. Jake.

441
00:39:17,520 --> 00:39:19,190
I need to go change for supper.

442
00:39:19,490 --> 00:39:21,090
Will you be dining with us?

443
00:39:21,420 --> 00:39:22,790
I can't stay out late.

444
00:39:23,120 --> 00:39:25,130
Suppers at 5:30

445
00:39:26,390 --> 00:39:28,630
Well that's pretty early

446
00:39:29,100 --> 00:39:32,000
The fact we are not all eight years of olds seems 
to have eluded Ms. Peregrine

447
00:39:32,830 --> 00:39:36,670
You can borrow some of Abe's clothes. His room's in the attic

448
00:39:47,320 --> 00:39:48,650
Jake

449
00:39:49,020 --> 00:39:51,450
Come meet Enoch, properly.

450
00:40:01,230 --> 00:40:04,300
Well, you must feel pretty out of place.

451
00:40:05,270 --> 00:40:08,300
Don't worry. I am used to it.

452
00:40:08,740 --> 00:40:11,410
I wasn't worried. Some advice for you though.

453
00:40:11,870 --> 00:40:13,310
Man to man

454
00:40:13,710 --> 00:40:16,140
If you think you're staying just because you like Emma,

455
00:40:16,480 --> 00:40:17,610
Don't bother

456
00:40:18,010 --> 00:40:21,680
You see she swore off romance years ago when 
she got her heart broken

457
00:40:22,150 --> 00:40:24,690
And she's never gonna change her mind.

458
00:40:27,920 --> 00:40:30,390
Enoch, I wasn't....

459
00:40:31,530 --> 00:40:33,590
What are you doing?

460
00:41:03,160 --> 00:41:04,860
Isn't he amazing?

461
00:41:05,230 --> 00:41:06,790
What did you do?

462
00:41:07,200 --> 00:41:08,560
This?

463
00:41:09,130 --> 00:41:11,270
Jake. This is not even the fun part.

464
00:41:11,670 --> 00:41:13,830
Do you want to see the fun part?

465
00:41:37,360 --> 00:41:39,160
They are like puppets.

466
00:41:40,200 --> 00:41:43,200
Just do anything I tell them.

467
00:41:44,100 --> 00:41:45,670
It is even more fun with people

468
00:41:46,400 --> 00:41:48,640
You should have seen some of the epic battles I used to have

469
00:41:48,800 --> 00:41:51,370
Emma ***********

470
00:41:53,170 --> 00:41:56,380
You need a necktie.

471
00:42:03,080 --> 00:42:06,620
So. What did my grandpa do when he was traveling?

472
00:42:07,160 --> 00:42:08,990
Visited other loops.

473
00:42:09,420 --> 00:42:10,760
Really?

474
00:42:11,130 --> 00:42:12,490
To do what?

475
00:42:13,030 --> 00:42:16,230
Jake, there are some questions I can't answer, alright?

476
00:42:16,830 --> 00:42:21,570
So it will be a lot easier for me if you just 
stopped asking them.

477
00:42:40,390 --> 00:42:41,960
Hey, what are you doing?

478
00:42:42,560 --> 00:42:44,590
Miller, go and put some clothes on.

479
00:42:45,190 --> 00:42:47,430
Polite persons do not take the sup in the nude!

480
00:42:47,800 --> 00:42:49,660
Alright!

481
00:42:52,200 --> 00:42:54,840
You can sit here Jake.

482
00:42:56,500 --> 00:42:59,310
Look at Enoch. He's jealous.

483
00:42:59,810 --> 00:43:01,540
Why would I be jealous?

484
00:43:02,010 --> 00:43:03,780
All of you can go marry Jake for all I care.

485
00:43:04,210 --> 00:43:08,250
Do not be mean, Enoch. She doesn't want to. 
She's just excited to a visitor.

486
00:43:08,680 --> 00:43:10,380
Nobody is marrying anybody.

487
00:43:10,790 --> 00:43:14,090
Now eat up your food before it gets cold.

488
00:43:16,990 --> 00:43:18,530
Hugh

489
00:43:19,590 --> 00:43:21,560
Where's your net?

490
00:43:34,510 --> 00:43:36,340
It must be very strange for you Jake.

491
00:43:36,950 --> 00:43:38,810
To meet your grandfather's friends.

492
00:43:39,280 --> 00:43:40,750
Visiting another century.

493
00:43:41,150 --> 00:43:42,750
There spaceships in your time, Jake.

494
00:43:42,880 --> 00:43:44,320
Like the Flash Gordon books?

495
00:43:44,790 --> 00:43:47,820
Now! Now! Olive, what did I say about the questions.

496
00:43:48,290 --> 00:43:49,690
We don't discuss the future here.

497
00:43:50,060 --> 00:43:53,060
We enjoy living in the here and now

498
00:43:55,300 --> 00:43:57,460
Claire, why aren't you eating?

499
00:43:57,870 --> 00:43:59,630
She's embarassed in front of Jake.

500
00:43:59,930 --> 00:44:02,500
Don't be, please.

501
00:44:19,490 --> 00:44:21,590
So, Jake, what is your peculiarity?

502
00:44:22,320 --> 00:44:24,630
Oh, I'm... I'm not peculiar.

503
00:44:25,160 --> 00:44:27,560
And that my friends is why he'll not be staying with us.

504
00:44:28,000 --> 00:44:30,300
No matter how hard we try to persuade him.

505
00:44:30,670 --> 00:44:33,100
We've spoken about this, Jake is just visiting.

506
00:44:33,470 --> 00:44:36,170
Do you not want to stay, Jake?

507
00:44:36,540 --> 00:44:37,870
Tonight or ..

508
00:44:38,170 --> 00:44:40,210
Forever. You should stay forever.

509
00:44:40,610 --> 00:44:42,910
Why would he if he doesn't have to?

510
00:44:43,240 --> 00:44:46,750
He can live out there. Grow older and have a good time instead.

511
00:44:47,150 --> 00:44:49,780
And leave. Just like his grandfather did.

512
00:44:54,660 --> 00:44:55,790
Emma!

513
00:44:56,090 --> 00:44:58,130
Excuse me, where she's going?

514
00:44:58,490 --> 00:44:59,830
That wasn't nice, Enoch!

515
00:45:00,130 --> 00:45:01,930
You know perfectly well why Abe left us.

516
00:45:02,260 --> 00:45:03,460
To join the army.

517
00:45:03,830 --> 00:45:07,730
And then he met a lady. And had a nice wedding cake.And a lovely little baby.

518
00:45:08,200 --> 00:45:10,000
Children!

519
00:45:11,010 --> 00:45:13,110
I know you'd all like a new friend

520
00:45:13,480 --> 00:45:16,340
But I'm sure Jake has plenty of his own back in  Florida.

521
00:45:19,750 --> 00:45:23,450
I think you should all get ready for movie-time while I answer that

522
00:45:24,090 --> 00:45:26,890
But you always let us stay for it.

523
00:45:44,740 --> 00:45:47,010
Hi. this is Abe.

524
00:45:47,480 --> 00:45:49,910
How is everyone?

525
00:45:55,780 --> 00:45:57,480
Yours has extra marshmallows, Jake.

526
00:45:57,950 --> 00:46:00,020
Miller, put some pajamas on.

527
00:46:00,290 --> 00:46:01,620
It is very hot in here

528
00:46:01,960 --> 00:46:04,420
Stop moaning.
Excuse me.

529
00:46:12,870 --> 00:46:14,800
My grandpa told me about this.

530
00:46:15,340 --> 00:46:17,200
Horace projects his dreams, right?

531
00:46:17,640 --> 00:46:19,310
He used to listen to the radio.

532
00:46:19,870 --> 00:46:22,380
Gets tedious when you know every word off by heart.

533
00:46:25,550 --> 00:46:27,550
Splendid, I'll take it.

534
00:46:27,980 --> 00:46:29,650
It sounds about clothes mostly.

535
00:46:29,980 --> 00:46:31,690
Delighted to meet you

536
00:46:32,290 --> 00:46:34,490
Super shirt by the way.

537
00:46:36,720 --> 00:46:38,790
When did he dream this?

538
00:46:39,060 --> 00:46:40,260
Last night

539
00:46:40,600 --> 00:46:42,360
Some of his dreams are prophetic

540
00:46:42,730 --> 00:46:45,370
But mostly they are about clothes.

541
00:46:45,730 --> 00:46:49,300
Prophetic as in, he can see into the future?

542
00:47:03,180 --> 00:47:06,950
The Ymbryne. Who is she? Mrs. Peregrine, you know her?

543
00:47:07,420 --> 00:47:10,490
Don't be silly. Horace was just having a bad dream. Thats all

544
00:47:44,660 --> 00:47:47,390
Thats quite enough. Thank you Horace.

545
00:47:47,930 --> 00:47:49,800
I think probably get going

546
00:47:50,170 --> 00:47:54,400
You could stay the night. If you wanted to. 
Rather than walk home in the dark.

547
00:47:55,070 --> 00:47:57,600
But the island is very safe, isn't it?

548
00:47:57,970 --> 00:47:59,270
Of course

549
00:47:59,840 --> 00:48:02,040
I only meant the path is dreadfully bumpy.
Jake could trip.

550
00:48:02,610 --> 00:48:08,220
Perhaps you could show him the shortcuts? 
Should he ever need to avoid...bumps.

551
00:48:08,720 --> 00:48:12,290
Wont you stay to see the restart. It is really quite spectacular.

552
00:50:55,720 --> 00:50:56,880
What was that?

553
00:50:57,290 --> 00:50:58,890
It was my phone.

554
00:50:59,550 --> 00:51:01,870
It's been dead the whole time in the loop I guess now ...

555
00:51:02,160 --> 00:51:03,760
Your phone?

556
00:51:04,130 --> 00:51:08,830
Yeah, ****** like a telephone? You can call people...

557
00:51:09,260 --> 00:51:12,670
And send written messages.

558
00:51:13,470 --> 00:51:15,240
Right. You'll love this. You can take a picture.

559
00:51:15,640 --> 00:51:17,810
Press that... there...yeah.

560
00:51:18,570 --> 00:51:20,170
See?

561
00:51:27,120 --> 00:51:29,120
Whats wrong?

562
00:51:31,920 --> 00:51:36,790
Its just funny to think that one day you'll grow up
 like Abe did.

563
00:51:37,190 --> 00:51:39,360
Get married... have children.

564
00:51:39,790 --> 00:51:41,460
Grandchildren

565
00:51:41,860 --> 00:51:44,900
You might even******* photograph.

566
00:51:45,330 --> 00:51:47,970
And I'll still be here.

567
00:51:48,570 --> 00:51:50,700
Wha... can you leave some day?

568
00:51:51,170 --> 00:51:53,470
And live in the present if you wanted to?

569
00:51:53,780 --> 00:51:59,410
No. More than a few minutes in your time 
and the years would catch up

570
00:51:59,880 --> 00:52:02,120
You'd age?

571
00:52:02,650 --> 00:52:03,920
Would... you're...

572
00:52:09,820 --> 00:52:12,060
I think it is the Ymbryne from Horace's dream.

573
00:52:12,730 --> 00:52:15,130
Are you sure it's not just a bird?

574
00:52:15,560 --> 00:52:17,230
I mean, I don't know... wouldn't it change?

575
00:52:17,570 --> 00:52:20,270
She can't. Not if she's hurt.

576
00:52:20,600 --> 00:52:24,070
I need to take her inside. You should go.

577
00:52:26,170 --> 00:52:29,710
Please do not say anything else. I hate goodbyes

578
00:52:32,310 --> 00:52:34,410
I'll come back tomorrow

579
00:52:34,720 --> 00:52:38,390
There's no hurry. I'll be here forever.

580
00:52:45,560 --> 00:52:46,690
Hey.

581
00:52:48,300 --> 00:52:50,830
Have I been all this damn island Where the hell were you?

582
00:52:51,330 --> 00:52:53,300
I was just on my way back.

583
00:52:53,670 --> 00:52:55,700
Sorry, I lost track of time.

584
00:52:55,840 --> 00:52:57,570
I was having a blast with Worm....

585
00:52:58,110 --> 00:52:59,310
and Dirty D?

586
00:52:59,610 --> 00:53:01,340
Dirty D?

587
00:53:02,040 --> 00:53:04,240
You know what? This is... this is good

588
00:53:04,550 --> 00:53:07,780
This is healthy. This is you're making real friends

589
00:53:08,380 --> 00:53:10,520
Doing teenage stuff.

590
00:53:10,850 --> 00:53:13,326
I think this is normal. I am sure that Dr. Golan will approve.

591
00:53:13,350 --> 00:53:14,660
Hey, you American

592
00:53:14,960 --> 00:53:16,720
Get over here

593
00:53:18,130 --> 00:53:22,300
Hey look here there they are, theres D-bag and worm-man

594
00:53:22,660 --> 00:53:24,330
Did you do this?

595
00:53:24,830 --> 00:53:27,400
What? No!

596
00:53:28,000 --> 00:53:29,340
Of course not

597
00:53:29,700 --> 00:53:31,170
It wasn't us.

598
00:53:31,770 --> 00:53:34,410
Listen Sir, I don't know what happened here but my son 
and his friends

599
00:53:34,740 --> 00:53:38,180
Have been together all day. 
And Jake would never do anything like this.

600
00:53:38,480 --> 00:53:40,280
Bollocks! We haven't seen him!

601
00:53:40,580 --> 00:53:44,080
You paid us yesterday. 
Why would we hang out with him today for free?

602
00:53:45,950 --> 00:53:48,820
Jake were you with them or not?

603
00:53:50,160 --> 00:53:52,890
No! I'm sorry!

604
00:53:53,600 --> 00:53:56,500
And you don't seriously think I could do this?

605
00:53:57,000 --> 00:53:59,500
I think we're done here, sir.

606
00:54:00,030 --> 00:54:02,070
Well, can pass on a message for me?

607
00:54:02,540 --> 00:54:06,540
Can you tell Dr. Golan that if she hadn't encouraged this cockamamie trip

608
00:54:06,840 --> 00:54:12,350
maybe my son wouldn't be mopping around all day in a derelict house
HAVING A GODDAMN BREAKDOWN.

609
00:54:12,780 --> 00:54:13,780
Hello?

610
00:54:13,920 --> 00:54:16,150
Dad, I'm not.

611
00:54:16,450 --> 00:54:17,580
I'm fine

612
00:54:18,020 --> 00:54:19,750
You're not.

613
00:54:20,220 --> 00:54:22,620
You are not fine. Jake.

614
00:54:23,220 --> 00:54:26,390
Coming here was a terrible... terrible idea.

615
00:54:26,730 --> 00:54:28,300
Im sorry, I lied ..

616
00:54:29,200 --> 00:54:31,470
Set your alarm for 8:00 am.

617
00:54:32,070 --> 00:54:33,730
I want to get to the beach early.

618
00:54:34,070 --> 00:54:38,140
The rest of the time left on this crap-o-island, 
we're stickin together.

619
00:54:38,910 --> 00:54:40,270
Where are you going?

620
00:54:40,610 --> 00:54:42,680
Downstairs for a drink.

621
00:55:30,990 --> 00:55:34,130
Dearest Peregrine: I don't wish to alarm you...

622
00:55:34,530 --> 00:55:37,430
but one of my informants sent me this.

623
00:55:37,970 --> 00:55:42,640
It would appear that some of Mr. Barron's group were in Black Pool, England.

624
00:55:43,440 --> 00:55:47,640
If I recall, Ms. Avocet has a loop there. "

625
00:55:48,180 --> 00:55:52,050
Please warn her and suggest that she make a new one right away. "

626
00:55:52,410 --> 00:55:53,610
Well hidden. "

627
00:55:53,920 --> 00:56:01,020
And take the greatest care yourself. With Love, Abe. January 2016

628
00:56:18,670 --> 00:56:21,740
Who is ready to hit the beach?

629
00:56:26,880 --> 00:56:29,050
Oh my goodness

630
00:56:29,580 --> 00:56:31,120
Unbelievable!

631
00:56:31,850 --> 00:56:33,950
Im right in the middle of a nesting are?

632
00:56:34,390 --> 00:56:36,520
What kind of idiot does that?

633
00:56:37,660 --> 00:56:40,990
Actually, the main nesting area is over there.

634
00:56:41,460 --> 00:56:42,860
I can show you, if you like.

635
00:56:43,200 --> 00:56:45,440
It's marvellous to meet a fellow bird-spotter!

636
00:56:45,670 --> 00:56:47,230
John Lamont.
Franklyn Portman.

637
00:56:47,600 --> 00:56:48,900
This is my son, Jake.

638
00:56:49,240 --> 00:56:50,770
John Newmont.

639
00:56:51,110 --> 00:56:52,940
That's a hell of a camera you got there.

640
00:56:53,370 --> 00:56:55,610
Oh, thank you, is absolutely fantastic.

641
00:56:56,080 --> 00:56:58,520
I am here to do some snaps for a book I'm writing.

642
00:56:58,850 --> 00:57:02,450
So, you gentlemen are here on holiday?

643
00:57:12,390 --> 00:57:14,660
So, you are not coming to the beach today?

644
00:57:15,000 --> 00:57:16,260
What's the point?

645
00:57:16,630 --> 00:57:21,740
That guys gonna cover ****** on some big glossy book, 
no ones even wanna look at mine.

646
00:57:22,770 --> 00:57:25,540
I might just have a nice afternoon nap.

647
00:57:26,170 --> 00:57:28,690
I do not suppose you saw uncle Oggie on you travels this morning,
 did you?

648
00:57:29,040 --> 00:57:31,010
He's usually here by now.

649
00:57:31,350 --> 00:57:32,650
I could go look for him.

650
00:57:32,950 --> 00:57:35,080
You're not going anywhere

651
00:58:09,980 --> 00:58:13,450
Jake, you're back! Come and play!

652
00:58:16,790 --> 00:58:18,960
I need to see to Ms. Peregrine first.

653
00:58:19,330 --> 00:58:21,200
Do you know where she is?

654
00:58:25,600 --> 00:58:28,400
Jake, you're back. How wonderful!

655
00:58:28,940 --> 00:58:30,500
How's it doing?

656
00:58:31,010 --> 00:58:32,770
Emma said it was an Ymbryne.

657
00:58:33,140 --> 00:58:36,280
She, not 'it'. Ymbrynes are always female.

658
00:58:36,640 --> 00:58:39,350
And Emma was quite correct. This is Ms. Avocet

659
00:58:39,780 --> 00:58:42,880
Her loop is in Black Pool England.

660
00:58:44,990 --> 00:58:47,420
That was a private letter, Jake.

661
00:58:49,960 --> 00:58:52,590
Who is Mr Barron?

662
00:58:53,760 --> 00:58:57,660
Ms. Peregrine, if my grandpa was involved with dangerous people

663
00:58:58,070 --> 00:59:00,370
I need to tell the police.

664
00:59:00,740 --> 00:59:02,500
To the police?

665
00:59:03,000 --> 00:59:05,840
Are you implying Abe died an unnatural death?

666
00:59:06,210 --> 00:59:09,140
I found him in the woods with eyes missing.

667
00:59:09,810 --> 00:59:13,080
I'd say that was pretty unnatural.

668
00:59:16,480 --> 00:59:19,650
Unless essential. I don't discuss unpleasant matters.

669
00:59:20,120 --> 00:59:22,890
An Ymbryne's is a duty to protect children, Jake.

670
00:59:23,490 --> 00:59:25,560
I am not a child

671
00:59:26,230 --> 00:59:28,930
He wanted you to tell me everything.

672
00:59:33,200 --> 00:59:35,840
Oh. How frustrating for you.

673
00:59:36,400 --> 00:59:39,840
Between Ms. Peregrine rules and my ******* not to scare you off

674
00:59:40,340 --> 00:59:42,440
It's like no ones telling you anything?!

675
00:59:43,010 --> 00:59:45,180
So why don't you then?

676
00:59:45,510 --> 00:59:47,350
It's not like you want me here

677
00:59:47,650 --> 00:59:48,780
Enoch, you can't

678
00:59:49,050 --> 00:59:50,620
You promised

679
00:59:50,950 --> 00:59:52,390
Olive is right

680
00:59:52,790 --> 00:59:55,760
However, I know someone who can break the rules.

681
00:59:56,160 --> 00:59:58,460
Want to meet him?

682
00:59:58,490 --> 01:00:01,260
Enoch, do not do this! Please

683
01:00:01,800 --> 01:00:05,230
You didn't want us to spend time together. That's what you said.

684
01:00:07,240 --> 01:00:09,540
Well, here we all are.

685
01:00:10,000 --> 01:00:11,810
Move, Olive

686
01:00:12,210 --> 01:00:15,880
If you're going to be like then I do not want to be your friend.

687
01:00:18,210 --> 01:00:22,250
Enoch! Leave Victor alone. It really upsets Bromwyn.

688
01:00:22,750 --> 01:00:25,850
Stop fussing, Fiona. Don't you think Jake should meet everybody?

689
01:00:26,150 --> 01:00:27,766
He's trying to frighten you away, Jake.

690
01:00:27,790 --> 01:00:30,190
He was always jealous of Abe and now he's jealous of you.

691
01:00:30,360 --> 01:00:33,130
Come and play with us instead

692
01:00:36,530 --> 01:00:39,570
I'd quite like to meet Victor

693
01:00:45,270 --> 01:00:47,210
After You.

694
01:00:55,320 --> 01:00:56,980
Hello Victor.

695
01:00:57,450 --> 01:01:01,390
I'm Jake. Im sorry to disturb....

696
01:01:04,430 --> 01:01:05,930
He can't hear you

697
01:01:31,090 --> 01:01:35,660
Hello Jake, I'm Victor. Do you want to know what killed me?

698
01:01:42,530 --> 01:01:46,270
Ah, there you are. ****** Its time for our daily walk.

699
01:01:49,170 --> 01:01:53,539
Emma, Who killed Victor? Was it the people with the white eyes?

700
01:01:53,540 --> 01:01:57,640
I asked you not to ask questions. 
I saw one the night my grandpa died.

701
01:02:01,420 --> 01:02:06,549
If it really was one, you have to tell Ms. Peregrinee. 
Could you recognize you recognize him from a photograph?

702
01:02:06,550 --> 01:02:12,560
Do you have one? Then come on. Theres somewhere I go to be alone.
I have things there.

703
01:02:50,100 --> 01:02:53,530
Is this the place?
No. This is how we get there.

704
01:03:13,220 --> 01:03:16,790
Emma! Your shoes! Lead shoes!

705
01:05:18,580 --> 01:05:23,680
Welcome to my secret hideout. 
How? How did you...

706
01:05:24,350 --> 01:05:30,060
Air. My peculiarity. It does what I want

707
01:05:49,380 --> 01:05:54,620
Jake. Before your grandfather retired, 
he asked me to keep this safe

708
01:06:12,270 --> 01:06:16,200
This is my grandpa's old map. 
It shows you where the loops are.

709
01:06:26,610 --> 01:06:33,750
That's him, thats the man I saw. Who is he? 
Thats Barron. He is the Leader.

710
01:06:35,120 --> 01:06:42,330
Leader of what? Who are these people? 
Bad people... bad peculiars.

711
01:06:43,570 --> 01:06:48,340
Abe dedicated his life to hunting them down. 
These are the ones he never found

712
01:06:49,100 --> 01:06:51,710
What do you mean "hunting"?

713
01:06:53,980 --> 01:07:00,979
They raided homes. Whole homes full of children left for dead. 
Abe took lives ...

714
01:07:00,980 --> 01:07:05,220
To save lifes. 
He only retired when you were born to protect you.

715
01:07:05,820 --> 01:07:13,820
From what? 
If I tell you the rest, you have to promise not to run away.

716
01:07:15,800 --> 01:07:23,800
Jake, you belong here. 
You know that I dont. I'm not like you. I'm just ordinary

717
01:07:24,410 --> 01:07:30,340
Maybe not Jake. only a peculiar can enter a time loop.

718
01:07:32,780 --> 01:07:42,780
No, that can't be right. I mean... I would know.
Fine. Then I'll show you something else.

719
01:07:49,800 --> 01:07:51,130
Hurry! You'll miss it.

720
01:08:04,710 --> 01:08:08,449
Ymbrynes usually pick the perfect date to create a loop. 
Now Ms. Peregrinee ..

721
01:08:08,450 --> 01:08:12,789
Had to do this in a rush. 
Why?

722
01:08:12,790 --> 01:08:18,589
Because the Germans were about to drop a bomb on the house. 
The point is, September the 3rd, 1943....

723
01:08:18,590 --> 01:08:24,030
wasn't perfect. The thing that killed Victor came back.

724
01:08:50,760 --> 01:08:53,660
Wait, watch out! ***********

725
01:09:21,990 --> 01:09:29,990
You can see it, can't you? No one else can. Its invisible, Jake.
 That was Abe's greatest gift of all.

726
01:09:33,330 --> 01:09:35,740
He could see the monsters.

727
01:09:40,140 --> 01:09:44,649
We call them 'Holocaust'. Hollows. for short.

728
01:09:44,650 --> 01:09:50,549
My grandpa told me about people, who turn into monsters. 
Is that what they are?

729
01:09:50,550 --> 01:09:56,519
I will explain everything, Jake. I fear its my duty now considering... but you should know that in doing so....

730
01:09:56,520 --> 01:10:03,560
I'm breaking a solemn promise. 
I knew you were peculiar when you were born but your grandfather....

731
01:10:03,570 --> 01:10:08,699
forbid me to tell you anything. 
His dearest wish was for you to have an ordinary childhood.

732
01:10:08,700 --> 01:10:14,239
Well I definitely had that. 
He intended to tell you the truth when you turned 18.

733
01:10:14,240 --> 01:10:21,350
He hoped his bed-time stories would pave the way.
Here's my book.

734
01:10:33,460 --> 01:10:40,230
Many years ago, a splinter faction emerged among our people

735
01:10:40,240 --> 01:10:44,269
Disaffected peculiars tired of living in loops. 
That's Mr. Barron.

736
01:10:44,270 --> 01:10:49,379
He believed that by harnessing the essence of an Ymbryne's powers,  
he and his cronies

737
01:10:49,380 --> 01:10:56,280
Could gain immortality and be able to live outside loops. 
He devised an experiment.

738
01:10:58,950 --> 01:11:04,290
He kidnapped an Ymbryne not knowing or caring 
Whether she would survive the experiment

739
01:11:25,150 --> 01:11:29,780
But the fate of Barron and his group
was more horrifying still.

740
01:12:06,220 --> 01:12:08,820
Why didn't Barron turn into one?

741
01:12:21,640 --> 01:12:28,740
He did.
But years later he found a way to reverse the effects...
to regain humanity.

742
01:12:29,080 --> 01:12:33,068
They had become not immortal gods - but Hollows.

743
01:12:33,080 --> 01:12:37,080
invisible beasts, dangerous, cold-blooded, deadly!

744
01:12:37,390 --> 01:12:41,720
Remember I told you they raided loops? This is why

745
01:12:42,060 --> 01:12:48,800
Barron discovered that by consuming the eyes of other peculiars ... especially children,

746
01:12:55,840 --> 01:12:57,770
He began to change

747
01:13:15,620 --> 01:13:18,990
Consume enough, and a hollow can fully regain its human form

748
01:13:21,100 --> 01:13:23,560
Just as Barron and some of his friends did.

749
01:13:32,710 --> 01:13:39,979
The rest of them are stuck as Hollows. 
Are you saying that Barron ate my uncle's ...

750
01:13:39,980 --> 01:13:46,090
He needs no more eyes himself, but I fear I led a Hollow to your grandfather, yes.

751
01:13:47,890 --> 01:13:53,690
After the first attacks on Loops, we all got better at hiding ...making new loops... keeping our

752
01:13:53,700 --> 01:13:59,399
Whereabouts secret.
 The Hollows grow more desparate every year 
and Barron wishes to help his friends

753
01:13:59,400 --> 01:14:03,540
Miss Peregrine! Come quickly! Miss Avocet's awake.

754
01:14:11,750 --> 01:14:17,989
Oh Miss Peregrine! They found my new loop. The children... 
I tried to save them but there were so many Hollows...

755
01:14:17,990 --> 01:14:24,790
I dont know how I escaped. 
You are safe now.

756
01:14:24,960 --> 01:14:28,660
None of us are safe. They set up the machine in my loop.

757
01:14:28,830 --> 01:14:33,129
They put in in the celler at Blackboat tower. They're still there... 
The machine?

758
01:14:33,130 --> 01:14:39,009
The experiment. They intend to do it again! This time, he's using more Ymbrynes.

759
01:14:39,010 --> 01:14:41,380
He still wants to be immortal

760
01:14:44,650 --> 01:14:52,650
Do Hollows only attack peculiars? 
Of course not! They're monsters, Jake, 
they'll slaughter anything in their path.

761
01:14:53,050 --> 01:14:58,230
Well, some sheep on the island were killed, 
You don't think they're here already, do you?

762
01:14:58,560 --> 01:15:06,560
Have you seen anyone with white eyes? 
I'm sorry children, we can't remain here.

763
01:15:07,200 --> 01:15:10,700
What? 
We leave on the first ferry, off the island tomorrow.

764
01:15:10,710 --> 01:15:14,270
Pack anything of importance. 
I'll make sandwiches and lead you to bed

765
01:15:14,280 --> 01:15:16,979
Are we leaving for good? When are we coming back?

766
01:15:16,980 --> 01:15:19,809
Never. If Ms. Peregrine's not here to reset the loop 
tomorrow night ...

767
01:15:19,810 --> 01:15:22,719
the house gets bombed. What? Our house?

768
01:15:22,720 --> 01:15:25,820
Dont cry, Miss Peregrine will find you another lovely house....
somewhere else

769
01:15:33,730 --> 01:15:37,760
Once this loop closes, that's it! 
I can't get back to my own time

770
01:15:37,770 --> 01:15:43,199
You didn't seem very happy there. I can't just leave! 
I have a family

771
01:15:43,200 --> 01:15:47,239
And you felt ordinary. Like nothing you do changes anything

772
01:15:47,240 --> 01:15:53,209
And, now you have a chance to do something that changes 
everything it all! Jake, we are in danger ...

